imud-influxdb (1.8.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix: /etc/imud/imud-influxdb.conf carries an InfluxDB API token and
    installed mode 0644, so every local user could read it — despite the
    SECURITY comment in the file telling the operator to restrict it. It
    is now 0640 root:imud, on upgrade over an existing 0644 file as well
    as on first install. The pristine template under
    /usr/share/doc/imud-influxdb/examples/ stays 0644.
  * Fix: a config file that exists but cannot be read is now fatal. It
    previously fell through to defaults, and since enabled defaults to
    false the bridge exited reporting "disabled in config
    ([imud-influxdb] enabled = false)" — naming the wrong cause entirely
    for what is a permissions problem, and the 0640 change above makes
    that the failure an operator is most likely to hit.
  * BEHAVIOUR CHANGE: the bridge now runs with imud as its primary group
    and no longer belongs to gpio. It carried Group=gpio only to reach
    the stream socket — it touches no hardware — and the socket is now
    imud:imud. The bridge connects as the socket's owner either way, so
    this needs no coordinated upgrade. It does mean the bridge can read
    its own 0640 root:imud config, which under Group=gpio it could not.
  * Harden: tier-2 systemd sandboxing (empty CapabilityBoundingSet, a
    @system-service syscall allow-list, RestrictNamespaces,
    LockPersonality, RestrictSUIDSGID, ProtectHostname, ProtectClock,
    ProtectProc=invisible, ProcSubset=pid, UMask=0077), and every fd is
    close-on-exec.
  * Requires wire format v17 (packet 276 bytes), unchanged since 1.7.
    Line protocol, field set, config keys and CLI are unchanged.

 -- Richard Simpson <richcreations@gmail.com>  Mon, 03 Aug 2026 12:00:00 -0700

imud-influxdb (1.7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Four new always-on fields from wire v17: innov_weight and
    innov_reject (MEKF update-gate health) and nis_accel and nis_mag
    (measurement-model consistency; 1.0 = the filter's covariance matches
    the innovations it sees, higher means over-confident).
  * The line-protocol buffer grows 768 -> 1024 bytes to fit the wider
    field set with headroom. An overflow returned n <= 0 and dropped the
    sample silently, so the margin matters.
  * Requires wire format v17 (packet 260 -> 276 bytes); must be upgraded
    together with the daemon.

 -- Richard Simpson <richcreations@gmail.com>  Mon, 27 Jul 2026 12:00:00 -0700

